You draw on your stamina, feeling strength return to your limbs as you use Second Wind. The pain recedes slightly — you're still hurt, but you can stand.

You swing your longsword at the wounded wisp, but the blade passes through its flickering form without finding purchase. The creature's AC is too high, and your strike misses.

The wounded wisp retaliates, but its lightning bolt crackles wide, missing you.

Round 2 begins. The first wisp lashes out with another arc of lightning. It strikes you, the current running through your armor, but the blow is weak — you take the hit but remain standing.

Then the third wisp strikes. A massive bolt of blue-white energy slams into you, and the world goes white. You feel your body convulse, your muscles lock, and then — nothing. You collapse to the stone floor, your shield clattering away, your longsword falling from nerveless fingers.

Darkness takes you. But deep within, you feel the Anvil Father's presence — a steadying warmth in the cold. You're not ready to die yet.

You're unconscious at 0 HP. You've made one death saving throw and succeeded. The three will-o'-wisps hover above you, their light pulsing. They haven't moved to finish you off yet — perhaps they're waiting, perhaps they're savoring it.

