Hessa considers your questions. "The records say the lightning was drawn to metal," she says. "The survivors who kept their weapons sheathed and avoided touching the blackvein walls fared better. The current arcs through the dark stone, they said. And the lights themselves — they're fast, Maren. Faster than a man can swing a hammer. Keep your distance if you can."

She pauses, thinking. "As for a guide... Torvin's brother, Dorin, works the upper levels. He knows the old adit — he's used it to check the ventilation shafts. He's not a fighter, but he knows the mountain's upper paths better than anyone alive. I can send for him."

She moves to the door and calls to a temple acolyte passing in the hall. "Find Dorin Stonecutter. Tell him Maren needs him at the old adit before dawn."

The acolyte nods and hurries away.

Hessa returns and moves to a storage closet, returning with a coil of hempen rope and a hooded lantern. "Take these," she says, handing you the rope and lantern.

You touch your holy symbol and cast Guidance, feeling the Anvil Father's steadying presence settle over you.

Hessa watches you prepare. "Dorin will meet you at the old adit. The climb is steep, but he knows the way. Be careful, Maren. The mountain remembers what was buried there."

